    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0857" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5161: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-05T21:00:00+08:00">May 5, 1932—9 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 5—1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Incident on Settlement border between Japanese marines and International
                        Settlement police involving 31st Infantry illustrates danger inherent in the
                        present situation. Commander in chief has informed Defense Committee that he
                        perceives no further occasion for continuance of state of emergency which is
                        now being used simply to keep Japanese out of Settlement and that American
                        forces are not here for that purpose. I approve of his action.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Commander in chief informed me that he is now informed that emergency will
                        probably be lifted tomorrow.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In view of this fact and the fact that Sino-Japanese agreement has been
                        signed and that Japanese evacuation will begin tomorrow, May 6th, I
                        recommend that reconsideration be given to the matter of the retention of
                        the 31st here at Shanghai and that that regiment be taken away. The British
                        have already reduced their forces by a <pb facs="0858" n="754"
                            xml:id="pg754"/> battalion. Commander in chief approves. Copy to
                        commander in chief and Consul General [at] Shanghai.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
